cards.back:
Modify existing rows.
UPDATE table SET col1 = val1 WHERE condition;
Always use WHERE to avoid updating all rows.

Remove rows from a table.
DELETE FROM table WHERE condition;
Without WHERE, deletes all rows.

Define a new table.
CREATE TABLE users (
  id INT PRIMARY KEY,
  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
);

Modify table structure.
ALTER TABLE table ADD column type;
ALTER TABLE table DROP COLUMN column;
ALTER TABLE table MODIFY column type;

Delete an entire table and its data.
DROP TABLE table;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS table;
Irreversible — use with caution.

Filter rows by condition.
SELECT * FROM orders WHERE amount > 100 AND status = 'active';
Operators: =, <>, >, <, >=, <=, LIKE, IN, BETWEEN, IS NULL

Sort results.
SELECT * FROM products ORDER BY price DESC, name ASC;
ASC (default) = ascending, DESC = descending.

Remove duplicate rows from results.
SELECT DISTINCT city FROM customers;
Applies to the entire row, not just one column.

Restrict number of returned rows.
SELECT * FROM products LIMIT 10 OFFSET 20;
PostgreSQL/MySQL syntax. SQL Server uses TOP.

Aggregate functions.
SELECT SUM(amount), AVG(amount), MIN(amount), MAX(amount) FROM orders;
Ignore NULL values.

Match any value in a list.
WHERE status IN ('active', 'pending');
Equivalent to multiple OR conditions. Can use subqueries.

Range condition (inclusive).
WHERE price BETWEEN 10 AND 50;
Equivalent to price >= 10 AND price <= 50.

Check for NULL values.
WHERE email IS NOT NULL;
Cannot use = or <> with NULL — they always return false.

A query inside another query.
SELECT * FROM products WHERE price > (SELECT AVG(price) FROM products);
Can be in WHERE, FROM, or SELECT.

Speed up queries on a column.
CREATE INDEX idx_name ON table(column);
Trade-off: faster reads, slower writes, more storage.

Ensures all values in a column are distinct.
CREATE TABLE users (email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE);
Allows one NULL (in most databases).

Prevents NULL values in a column.
name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL;
Enforced on INSERT and UPDATE.

Sets a default value for a column when none is provided.
status VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'pending';
created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Returns the first non-NULL argument.
SELECT COALESCE(nickname, first_name, 'Anonymous') FROM users;
Useful for fallback values.

Group operations atomically.
BEGIN;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE id = 1;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = 2;
COMMIT;

Remove all rows from a table quickly.
TRUNCATE TABLE logs;
Faster than DELETE (no row-by-row logging). Resets auto-increment. Cannot be rolled back in some DBs.
